{"name":"Wild Mustang","hex":"#695649","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"mustang","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, hardy, naturalized (feral) horse of the North American west.","A merchant marine who joined the U.S. Navy as a commissioned officer during the American Civil War."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt mustangs (wild horses), either for military use or for slaughter as pet food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mustang"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wild Mustang (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Mustang is a 1935 American Western film written and directed by Harry L. Fraser. The film stars Harry Carey, Barbara Fritchie, Del Gordon, Katheryn Johns, Bob Kortman, George Chesebro, Chuck Morrison, Dick Botiller, George Morrell\tand Milburn Morante. The film was released on October 22, 1935, by Ajax Pictures Corporation."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Wild_Mustang_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Mustang_(film)","wikidata":"Q18471858"},{"title":"Mustang","blocks":[{"text":"The mustang is a free-roaming horse of the Western United States, descended from horses brought to the Americas by the Spanish conquistadors. Mustangs are often referred to as wild horses, but because they descend from domesticated stock, they are formally classified as feral horses. The original mustangs were Colonial Spanish horses, but many other breeds and types of horses contributed to the modern mustang, now resulting in varying phenotypes. Some free-roaming horses are relatively unchanged from the original Spanish stock, most strongly represented in the most isolated populations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Mustanggelding.jpg/330px-Mustanggelding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mustang","wikidata":"Q211848"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/500px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/1280px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/500px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Horsescd1l-095.jpg/500px-Horsescd1l-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Horsescd1l-095.jpg/500px-Horsescd1l-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mustang mare and foal with stallion in the West Warm Springs HMA (Herd Management Area) in Oregon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorsescd1l-095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg/500px-Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mustang_Utah_2005_2.j